<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Restoration Druid Healer in Cataclysm Classic Pre-Raid. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from dungeons, reputations, and professions. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c4">Best in Slot Gear for Restoration Druid Healer in Pre-Raid</span></h2>Resto Druids see a few major changes to itemization in Cataclysm: all HoTs can now crit, and MP5 is no longer a stat (being replaced by Spirit instead). The latter doesn't really matter as very little of our gear had MP5 to begin with, but it does change some items.<br/>However, most importantly, Cataclysm brings armor specialization - which means that wearing all leather grants us 5% extra Int (which is also SP in Cata!) That means it's time to throw all of that gross cloth, leather's in fashion.<br/>
<br/>Overall, our primary gearing goals will be to focus haste breakpoints, then balance our mana regen with spirit. Afterwards, mastery tends to be slightly stronger than crit.<br/>Due to the stats available in pre-raid, as long as you have several 359s, hitting the 2005 haste breakpoint is fairly straightforward. If you mostly only have 346s though, it will be fairly hard to get there and may be better to stick to the 916 haste breakpoint instead.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Int - This stat now gives spellpower by itself, on top of the mana and crit that it continued to provide in WotLK. We now gem Int (it's a red gem now, just like SP was), unless you're trying to hit a specific Haste breakpoint.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Spirit - Our core regeneration stat. The 5 second rule is completely gone in Cataclysm, there's only "in combat" and "out of combat" regen.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - Haste now always affects all of our HoTs, even <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=33763/lifebloom">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_herb_felblossom.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lifebloom</span></a> - though at specific breakpoints, you GAIN an entire tick. This means that between breakpoints, Haste is a mana-negative, healing-positive stat, while every breakpoint adds a significant amount of mana efficiency.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - All of our HoTs can now crit, making this no longer a dead stat! Critical healing also does 200% healing in Cata, up from 150% in previous expansions. However, since the stat budget of critical strike rating on gear is pretty expensive, it's less effective for healing throughput increases than Mastery.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - This is a new stat that buffs all of our direct healing. Additionally as long as you cast one direct heal every 10s, it also buffs all HoTs an equal amount. For exclusively healing throughput, this is a great stat.</div></li></ol>
<div style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="absolute-pre-raid-bis">Absolute Pre-Raid BiS</h4>This is the best possible setup you could have before stepping into a single raid in Phase 1. However, this setup is obviously incredibly unrealistic as it not only requires two extremely rare world drops, it also requires 8000 Valor to put together (not including the boots!) While this is an aspirational setup, it is not very realistic and is here solely as an informative display of what can be achieved with only non-raid gear.<br/>
